course: dictionary
lesson: 7144
title: One word, three jobs: pepper
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the same spelling can do different jobs. Context tells you which meaning is right. «Please pass the salt and pepper.» Here pepper is a hot powder for food.
explain: «She chopped a red pepper and a green pepper for the salad.» Here pepper is a vegetable, and you can count peppers. Pepper as a spice is uncountable: you say some pepper, not two peppers.
explain: «A speech peppered with jokes» uses pepper as a verb. It means filled with many small things. Test it by putting «filled with» into the sentence: a speech filled with jokes still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Pepper can be a spice, a vegetable, or a verb: the same spelling, three different jobs.
fact: «Pepper» (spice) means a hot-tasting powder made from dried, crushed peppercorns, used to season food.
fact: «Pepper» (vegetable) means a hollow vegetable, red, green, yellow or orange, also called a bell pepper or capsicum.
fact: Some small peppers are hot, like chilli peppers, so wash your hands before you touch your eyes.
fact: Botanists call peppers fruits because they hold seeds. «In 1893 the US Supreme Court still ruled the tomato a vegetable for tax.»
exercise: In «Vitamin C, found in oranges, lemons, peppers and berries, helps the body heal», what are the peppers? | A kind of soap | Dried peppercorns in a jar | *Vegetables you can eat | A powder you shake onto food
exercise: «The speech was peppered with jokes.» What does peppered mean? | Cooked in a hot pan | *Filled with many small things | Hidden under a blanket | Shaken onto food
exercise: Mum says, «Pass the pepper, please.» What is the pepper here? | A red vegetable | *A hot powder made from crushed peppercorns | A kind of salt | A sharp knife
test: In the «pepper and soap» trick, what happens when soap touches the pepper? | It turns blue | *It rushes to the edges | Nothing happens at all | It melts into the water
test: «Wash your hands after cutting chilli peppers before you touch your eyes.» Why? | *They can burn | They make your hands grow | They help you see better | They are sticky sweets
exam: Which sentence uses pepper as a verb? | «The green pepper was crisp and fresh.» | «Add a pinch of pepper to the soup.» | *«The speech was peppered with jokes.»
